      <div type="clause" n="30">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 30</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="102" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXIIII. Gif mon cierliscne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.8-2"/> monnan fliemanfeorme teo, be his agnu<hi rend="italic">m<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.9-2"/></hi> were geladige he hine; gif he ne mæge, gielde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.10-2"/> hine his agne were; ⁊ se gesiðmon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.11-2"/> swa be his were.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="102" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXIIII. Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.2-2"/> cierliscne mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.2-2"/>, flymon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.2-2"/> feormie, ⁊ hine mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.2-2"/> teo, be his agenum were geladie he hine; gif he ne mæge, gilde (he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.1-2"/>) hine (be<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.1-2"/>) his agenan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.5"/> were; ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.2-2"/> se<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.6"/> gesiðmon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.2-2"/> (eac<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.1-2"/>) swa be his were.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="30" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="102" ed="#liebermann"/>Be þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe cyrlis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1a" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.1a"/> man feormige flyman. Gyf man cyrliscne mannan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.1"/> flymanfeormienne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.2"/> téo, be his ag<hi rend="italic">e</hi>non were geladige [he<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.3"/>] hine; gyf he ne mæge, gylde he hine be his agenu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> were; ⁊ se g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>siþmon eac swá be his were.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="30" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="103" ed="#liebermann"/>Si cyrliscus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.8"/> homo forsbanniti<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.9"/> firmationis accusetur, per suam ipsius<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.10"/> weram neget; si non possit, persoluat eum wera sua; et se<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.11"/> gesiþman etiam sic<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_30.lnote.oe.12"/> per weram suam.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="46" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be ðam þe cyrlisc<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_30.attnote.fn.1"/> man feormige flyman.] Gif mon cierliscne monnan<ptr type="editorNote" n="2" target="#Ine_30.attnote.fn.2"/> fliemanfeorme teo<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#Ine_30.attnote.fn.3"/>, be his agnum were geladige he hine; gif he ne mæge, gielde hine<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Ine_30.attnote.fn.4"/> his agne<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Ine_30.attnote.fn.5"/> were; ⁊ se gesiðmon [eac]<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#Ine_30.attnote.fn.6"/> swa be his were.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="30" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="396" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LXXIIII} Gif mon cierliscne monnan fliemanfeorme teo, be his agnu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> were geladige he hine; gif he ne mæge, gielde hine his agne were; ⁊ se gesiðmon swa be his were.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="103" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_30.lnote.de.1"/> einen gemeinfreien Mann der Friedlosen-Beherbergung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_30.lnote.de.2"/> zeiht, so reinige er sich [durch Eid] in Höhe seines eigenen Wergeldes. Wenn er [das] nicht vermag, so kaufe er<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_30.lnote.de.3"/> sich los<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_30.lnote.de.4"/> durch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_30.lnote.de.5"/> sein eigenes Wergeld; und der Mann vom [Königs]gefolge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_30.lnote.de.6"/> [schwöre sich von solcher Klage rein] (ebenfalls<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_30.lnote.de.7"/>) so gemäss seines Wergeldes.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If a common freeman is accused of harbouring outlaws, let him clear himself [by an oath] to the amount of his own wergeld. If he cannot [do that], let him buy himself free with his own wergeld; and the man of the [king’s] retinue [is to clear himself of such a charge] (likewise) according to his wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="47" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone accuses a commoner of harbouring a fugitive he shall clear himself by [an oath] equal in value to his own wergeld. If he cannot do so he shall pay for [harbouring] him [the fugitive], [a sum equal to] his own wergeld. A nobleman also shall pay according to the amount of his own wergeld.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="403" ed="#whitelock"/>If a <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> is accused of harbouring fugitives, he is to exculpate himself by [an oath of the amount of] his own wergild; if he cannot, he is to pay for [harbouring] him his own wergild; and the man of <hi rend="italic">gesith</hi> rank similarly by his wergild.<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#Ine_30.whinote.n.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="397" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a <hi rend="italic">ceorl</hi> is accused of harboring a fugitive, let him clear himself with [an oath equal to] his own <hi rend="italic">wer</hi>; if he cannot, let him compensate with his own <hi rend="italic">wer</hi>; and a nobleman likewise according to his [own] <hi rend="italic">wer</hi>.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IIEw_5-2">II Ew 5.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="397"><label>cited in</label> <ref target="clause:IIEw_5-2">II Ew 5.2</ref> <quote>Cited in ii Edward §5.2.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="268"><label>refers to</label> <ref target="clause:IIEw_5-2">II Ew 5.2</ref> <quote>The second of these provisions can be taken to refer to Ine's law on 'fliemanfeorm (fugitive harbouring)'</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="182"><label>cites; wording closer to rubric than to law</label> <ref target="clause:IIEw_5-2">II Ew 5.2</ref> <quote>the wording of Edward's supposed citation of Ine's law ('ðe flieman feormige') was actually closer to that of the rubric than to that of Ine's text</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.1a" n="1a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Endung</hi> an <hi rend="italic">radirt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ending an erased</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. geänd.</hi> -minge</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered in the 16th cent. to -minge</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. eingefügt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">inserted in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cirl. <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> schirl. <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cirl. T; schirl. Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">forsbati <hi rend="italic">Lond; verbessert</hi> forsbannati <hi rend="italic">Co; so Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">forsbati Lond; corrected to forsbannati Co; thus Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sege si <hi rend="italic">T;</hi> sepe si. <hi rend="italic">M Hk Br;</hi> se siþma <hi rend="italic">Lond; geänd.</hi> sapiens sic sit <hi rend="italic">Co Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sege si T; sepe si. M Hk Br; se siþma Lond; altered to sapiens sic sit Co Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sic per <hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond, wo</hi> wera sua</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic per lacking in Lond, which has wera sua</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">letztes</hi> a <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi>, n <hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">last a on an erasure, n written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sege sið mon <hi rend="italic">H</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sege sið mon H</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cyrl. man. flyman feorminge <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cyrl. man. flyman feorminge Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">agenum <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">agenum Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gylde he hine be his agenum <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gylde he hine be his agenum Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.oe.11-2" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-man eac swa <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-man eac swa Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Wenn jemand einen gemeinfreien Mann, einen Friedlosen, herbergt und man ihn verklagt’ verdrehend H, als hinge die Eidesschwere vom Stande des Friedlosen ab. So späteres Recht. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Begünstigung 2. 3; Wergeld 30h; Eidesschwere 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘If anyone harbours a common freeman, an outlaw, and he is accused’ H, distorting it, as though the weight of the oath depended on the rank of the outlaw. So later law. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Begünstigung 2. 3; Wergeld 30h; Eidesschwere 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dieser Satz scheint zitiert von II Ew 5, 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This sentence seems to be quoted by II Ew 5, 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hcor. modernisiert durch Ergänzung von Pronomen und Präposition</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hcor. modernises by supplying a pronoun and a preposition</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Von drohender Leibesstrafe; <hi rend="italic">vgl. o.</hi> 11⁶. Q und Neuere verstehen ‘bezahle er ihn’. Allein der 200-Schilling-Mann konnte nicht durch seine 200 Schilling etwa einen adligen Geächteten von 1200 loskaufen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">From threatened corporal punishment; <hi rend="italic">cf. above</hi> 11⁶. Q and more recent scholars understand ‘let him pay him’. But the 200-shilling man could not, with his 200 shillings, buy off, say, a noble outlaw worth 1200</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hcor. B modernisieren</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Hcor. B modernise</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q verstümmelt anderwärts das hier beibehaltene Wort oder übersetzt es verschieden. <hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> Gefolgsadel 4. 7a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Elsewhere Q mutilates the word retained here, or translates it in different ways. <hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> Gefolgsadel 4. 7a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_30.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zusatz Hcor. B. — ‘In Proportion’ heisst <hi rend="italic">and swa</hi> auch 34, 1. 54. — Nicht etwa neben dem Ceorl zahlt auch der <hi rend="italic">gesið</hi> als in Polizei unachtsam, wie Earle verstand</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Addition of Hcor. B. — <hi rend="italic">and swa</hi> means ‘in proportion’ also in 34, 1. 54. — It is not, say, that the <hi rend="italic">gesið</hi> also pays alongside the ceorl, as having been negligent in policing, as Earle understood it</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_30.attnote.fn.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>cyrlisc</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">cyrlis</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_30.attnote.fn.2" n="2" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>monnan</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">mon</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_30.attnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>teo</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">flymon feormie ⁊ hine mon teo</hi>. H. <hi rend="italic">flymanfeormienne teo</hi>. B. <hi rend="italic">-inge teo</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_30.attnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>hine</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">gilde</hi> (<hi rend="italic">he</hi>) <hi rend="italic">hine</hi> (<hi rend="italic">be</hi>). H* &amp; B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_30.attnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>agne</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">agenan</hi>. H. <hi rend="italic">agenum</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_30.attnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>eac</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">(<hi rend="italic">eac</hi>) <hi rend="italic">swa</hi>. H* &amp; B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ine_30.whinote.n.3" n="3" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">403</biblScope></bibl><label>wergild</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">i.e. if he is accused of this crime he swears or pays according to his wergild. On <hi rend="italic">gesith, see</hi> p. 396, n. 4.</seg></note>
      </div>
